# Container Queries Components

## Overview
Tailwind CSS v4 supports `@container` for component-level responsive design.

## Setup

```css
@container card (min-width: 24rem) {
  .card-title {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }
}
```

## Named Containers

```css
@theme {
  --container-card: 24rem;
}

.card {
  container-type: inline-size;
  container-name: card;
}
```

## Utility Variants

Use `@sm:/@md:/@lg:` syntax scoped to container.

```html
<div class="card">
  <h2 class="[container-card]@sm:text-lg">Title</h2>
  <p class="[container-card]@md:grid-cols-2">Content</p>
</div>
```

## Patterns

- Card adapts to parent width, not viewport
- Navigation switches layout at container size
- Grid components reflow based on available space
- Avoid nesting containers unnecessarily

## Best Practices

- Define container name for clarity
- Set `container-type: inline-size` on parent
- Combine with `min()` and `clamp()` for fluidity
- Test with narrow and wide containers
- Keep breakpoint names semantic
